WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.803
A successful payment is not a delivered order. Rehearsal
helps developers and quality assurance

00:00:06.803 --> 00:00:14.396
teams test transaction agents before delegation. It
combines controlled failures, isolated

00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:19.180
practice, policy review, and an independent commerce
ledger.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:29.104
The buyer is Amazon Nova two Lite on Bedrock, running
through Strands. It must deliver three tents

00:00:29.104 --> 00:00:36.685
and six lights within five hundred synthetic credits.
Medusa manages the commerce records. The

00:00:36.685 --> 00:00:40.923
browser observes those records and cannot buy anything.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.268
In a separate actual Nova run, a tool free reviewer
proposed refreshing quotes before ordering. We

00:00:50.268 --> 00:00:56.026
replayed that candidate from the same snapshot. Both
executions spent four hundred and thirty

00:00:56.026 --> 00:01:03.514
credits, so the proposal did not improve the result. A
later review returned an invalid field and

00:01:03.514 --> 00:01:12.547
the attempt was rejected. Initial buying, review, and
candidate testing share one budget. We retain

00:01:12.547 --> 00:01:15.229
rejected attempts and their costs.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.465
This is an actual Nova run against local Medusa, shown at
its original speed. The controller

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:32.617
changes supplier A stock during the session. Model
decisions pass through server checks before any

00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:39.919
order or payment. The browser shows the observed changes,
delivery status, and recorded execution

00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:48.894
decisions. A sealed execution log proves file consistency.
The separate export verifier establishes

00:01:48.894 --> 00:01:55.059
whether the goods arrived. After the recording ends, the
final frame is held.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.616
A different run failed. Stock disappeared after the A
order was created. Payment was rejected, and

00:02:10.616 --> 00:02:16.874
Nova repeatedly retried the same payment instead of
finding a valid recovery. It reached the

00:02:16.874 --> 00:02:24.664
deadline with nothing delivered. This failure remains in
the evidence. The earlier successful run

00:02:24.664 --> 00:02:28.124
does not establish recovery for every timing.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.396
A separate frozen batch had 20 planned executions per
method. The fixed rule baseline completed 15.

00:02:37.396 --> 00:02:44.687
The single model completed 11. The model with simulation
completed 8. Simulation with Peer Review

00:02:44.687 --> 00:02:52.837
completed 7. The entire batch recorded 2.31 US dollars in
model usage, including all learning and

00:02:52.837 --> 00:03:00.128
review. These samples do not establish a general Peer
Review advantage. Failed, rejected and

00:03:00.128 --> 00:03:03.623
impossible cases remain in every denominator.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.245
The source includes English testing instructions, the
architecture, and retained evidence. Local

00:03:13.245 --> 00:03:21.813
checks run on macOS and a same host Linux container.
Independent machine reproduction, held out

00:03:21.813 --> 00:03:29.104
generalization, and observed developer time savings remain
open. This proof of concept demonstrates

00:03:29.104 --> 00:03:35.141
bounded model execution and inspectable transaction
outcomes. It does not claim production

00:03:35.141 --> 00:03:42.003
readiness or better policies. A later clarification of
delivery waiting was tested in a separate

00:03:42.003 --> 00:03:54.612
known pilot. B0 4/5, B1 4/5, B2 3/5, B3 4/5. This is a
different test set, not proof of general

00:03:54.612 --> 00:03:55.599
improvement.
